1. Concept
One-liner: A cute pet-rescue bubble shooter. Shoot colored bubbles, match 3 or more, free puppies and kittens trapped inside bubbles, then collect them and bring them home.
Target market: United States, Canada, UK, Australia and Europe. iOS and Android, English at launch.
Why it can win
•	Dogs and kittens have broad appeal with Western casual players, and a collect-and-care loop gives them a reason to come back every day.
•	New levels every week and a weekly event keep the game fresh.
•	Light build (under 100 MB) with fast load times. Panda Pop is 274 MB.
•	Fewer forced ads, with rewarded ads as the main ad format.
2. Core loop
Aim → shoot → match 3+ → floating bubbles drop → goal met within the shot limit → stars + coins → next level.
Target session: 5 to 8 minutes, about 10 levels.
3. Level goals
•	Paw Points: reach a score within a limited number of shots.
•	Pet Rescue: free X puppies or kittens trapped inside bubbles by popping or dropping those bubbles.
•	Treat Collect: pop the bubbles next to bones and fish to collect a set number of treats.
•	Boss Level: a fixed wall with limited shots and a bigger reward.
Later levels combine two goals.
