Design rules
•	Introduce one new element every 2 to 3 levels.
•	Boss level every 10 levels.
•	Every 5th level is an easy gift level to keep players feeling good.
•	Aim for about an 85% win rate in the first 10 levels, falling to 55 to 65% on hard levels.
•	Store levels as JSON files so they can be tuned remotely without an app update.
7. Meta progression
•	Worlds: Backyard, Animal Shelter, Pet Town, each with its own art and music.
•	Collectible pets: original puppies and kittens, each with a small perk (e.g. +1 starting shot) and costumes to unlock. Collected from chests and events.
•	Pet Home: spend stars to decorate a home for your rescued pets and keep players returning.
•	Daily streak chest and a daily puzzle with the same layout for everyone and a leaderboard.
•	Weekly events: Adopt-a-Pet Week.
•	Lives: 5 lives that refill over time or through rewarded ads.
8. Monetization
Principles: free to play. Ads are rewarded, not forced.
Ads
•	Rewarded video: extra 5 shots, free booster, double coins, life refill.
•	Interstitials: none before level 15, then at most one every 3 levels, never mid-level.
•	Use ad mediation (e.g. AdMob plus a second network) to improve fill rate and ad revenue.
In-app purchases (prices are starting points to test)
Product	Idea	Starting price (USD)
Starter pack	Coins + 3 boosters, one-time	$1.99 to $2.99
Coin packs	4 to 5 tiers	$0.99 to $19.99
Season Pass	Free and premium reward track	$4.99 to $6.99
Remove Ads	One-time purchase	$4.99 to $7.99
Unlimited lives (1 hour / 1 day)	Impulse buy	$0.99 to $1.99
Test each price point with A/B tests during soft launch, since Western players respond strongly to starter-pack offers.
Payments: standard App Store and Google Play billing.
9. Tech and art
•	Engine: Unity 2D.
•	Targets: iOS and Android, 60 fps, base build under 100 MB. Download worlds on demand.
•	Backend: Firebase for analytics, remote config and cloud save.
•	Languages: English at launch. Add Spanish, French, German and Portuguese later.
•	Art: bright, soft cartoon style with original puppies and kittens. Do not copy Panda Pop's pandas or any existing pet game's characters.
9a. Look and feel
•	Top bar: pet icon with pets rescued, a 3-star progress bar, score and a pause button.
•	Board: glossy paw-print bubbles. Pets sit inside bubbles, and some levels are laid out as shapes such as a heart.
•	Hero: a cat or dog holds the next bubble in a blossom meadow, with a swap crate showing shots left, cheering pets on the side and locked booster slots at the bottom.
•	Style: bright, soft and glossy. All characters and art are original.
•	Playable prototype: Paw Pop prototype with 5 levels (score and pet rescue goals).
10. Starting KPI targets (validate in soft launch)
•	Day 1 retention: 35 to 40%
•	Day 7 retention: 10 to 15%
•	Average session: 6 to 8 minutes
•	Rewarded ad opt-in: 30%+ of daily active users
•	Level 10 completion: 60%+ of new installs
11. 8-week roadmap
